     "9dc6aa18-f362-4a7e-9e21-998f7c998332"], Cell["\<\
groups of generators with the degree above which their part of a monomial \
vanishes; empty when nothing is truncated\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"7dce1869-f1ef-4f1f-a7cd-7b457020cc7c"]}
  }]], "2ColumnTableMod",ExpressionUUID->"e459f64f-1acf-44c5-a5d5-\
3901403bba3a"],

Cell["\<\
The underlying algebra is the free graded commutative algebra on the \
generators: a generator of even degree is polynomial, and one of odd degree \
squares to zero.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"e0eb76c0-dbd7-4131-b318-673a05123cf9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A monomial is written as a product of generators and is read in the order \
the model declares them, so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"x", " ", "y"}]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "62e8af0c-f2d8-45cc-81f4-a0af9d7a25c7"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"y", " ", "x"}]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "fca6f671-6e55-4aba-ad60-e99ccf3746c4"],
 " are the same expression and denote the same monomial. The sign of a \
reordering is produced by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["SullivanModelProduct"]], 
    "paclet:ChernSimons/ref/SullivanModelProduct", 
    "ChernSimons Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "28878331-804f-44fc-8306-a1e21bd03186"],
 ", not by the way a monomial is typed."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"8a749bc7-6983-43ac-b224-7a8cb6df6d79"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["orientation", "TI"],
 " is either a monomial of degree ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "ee76945c-6a9e-4729-af87-33a5a1682893"],
 ", meaning the functional that is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["1", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "6e6e6499-a0b2-4d9a-9083-e3a8176b15c7"],
 " on it and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["0", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "7870df8f-2795-44a0-9350-9130eacd315a"],
 " on the other monomials of degree ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "d90a523f-05db-44c0-92b5-eb48bcccfe8b"],
 ", or an Association of numeric values on monomials of degree ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "4ab9da45-cec7-41d3-9a76-c39f4a936f4c"],
 ". Zero values are dropped."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"f6269848-75fc-485e-ba5f-b17843ded1fc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The orientation must be one in the sense of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["OrientationQ"]], "paclet:ChernSimons/ref/OrientationQ", 
    "ChernSimons Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "a4b29cfd-5549-4814-a5ae-08db18016c43"],
 ": it vanishes on the image of the differential and is nonzero on some \
cocycle of degree ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "8b872283-391a-4378-9510-7fe4867c2ece"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"9c7f85a4-bc7c-42e0-90f7-d27b882d340d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The result is a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["Failure"]], "paclet:ref/Failure"},
   "RefLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "5a2e1e85-77db-4fdd-b071-14d3ec1e8309"],
 " when the differential does not raise the degree by one or does not square \
to zero, and when the values do not define an orientation."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"5a574e2e-d870-4874-8f7e-6869a722359c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The default generator symbols are created in the current context: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "v"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"61cd6701-f413-46b7-ae56-15d4229f24ea"],
 " for the circle, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "a"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"0b3d468b-9502-4234-8fd6-fb7f845c1596"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "b"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"787ee8f6-57fb-4a32-9342-5cc55f6b8d4f"],
 " for a projective space, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "x"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"4f6daabc-8200-43bc-8270-6ec988d46c6e"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "y"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"a5ba78d6-0c06-42a9-aed8-b4198cf66def"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "z"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"c955e5be-3ed8-48af-b70c-92ca4d67ab99"],
 " for the Heisenberg nilmanifold, and so on. ",
 StyleBox["generators", "TI"],
 " chooses them, which is also how a collision is avoided when two models are \
tensored."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"c92aea63-6df7-45c3-a3de-a00b0aded937"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["truncation", "TI"],
 " is an integer, or ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["Infinity"]], "paclet:ref/Infinity"},
   "RefLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "cf368d7c-913c-4e7d-9f1b-549ab914b469"],
 " for no truncation, the default. The monomials above any degree span a \
differential graded ideal, since the differential raises the degree by one, \
so the quotient is again a differential graded algebra."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"cc4631b6-424f-47ec-b83e-f6bae0966833"],

Cell["\<\
In a tensor product the generators of the factors must be disjoint. The \
differentials and the truncations are joined, the orientations multiplied and \
the degrees added; each truncation stays with the generators of its factor.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"f2c2e387-a32e-4dc0-b522-f05286a9145b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Input of another shape returns unevaluated: a generator of degree ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["0", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "415c502a-e0b3-4ce1-966b-7e0a289d89b5"],
 ", a differential that is not a polynomial in the generators, a non-numeric \
orientation value, a tensor product whose factors share a generator, a \
catalogue parameter out of range."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"281cd0e5-fa69-45bf-ae85-48121c28b06d"]
}, Open  ]],

